# ─── Deny dot-paths by default (must stay first) ──────────────
# AG-GIT-DOTFILES (see BinHsu/aegis-template#5): a blocklist has to predict
# each credential dotfile before it exists, and misses most of them
# (.envrc, .netrc, .npmrc, .pypirc, .git-credentials, .ssh/, .docker/,
# .kube/, .gnupg/, .direnv/, .codex/, .mcp.json, .scratch/, ... — measured
# 14/18 unblocked). Default-deny + a small allowlist inverts that: only the
# directories named below can ever be committed.
#
# Trap 1 — position, not style: .gitignore is last-match-wins. This block
# MUST be the first thing in the file. Moving `.*` to the bottom (or adding
# a later bare exclude of one of the allowlisted dirs) silently re-ignores
# everything below, including .githooks/pre-commit itself. Verified: the
# same six lines appended at the end of this file re-excluded every path
# the allowlist is meant to protect.
#
# Trap 2 — negate directories, not files inside them: `!.claude/x` cannot
# rescue `x` while `.claude/`'s *parent match* (`.*`) still applies — git
# matches a no-slash pattern like `.*` against every path component, so an
# excluded ancestor wins regardless of a child-level negation. The
# allowlist below therefore negates the directories themselves
# (`!.claude/`), not files under them.
#
# Accepted cost: any other new dotfile or dot-directory (.editorconfig,
# .nvmrc, .npmrc if you genuinely need one committed, a future tool's
# config) is blocked until it gets its own `!` line here — add that line
# in the same commit that adds the file.
.*
!.gitignore
!.claude/
!.githooks/
!.github/
!.semgrep/
# Only the reviewed maintenance skill travels; other agent state stays ignored.
!/.agents/
/.agents/*
!/.agents/skills/
/.agents/skills/*
!/.agents/skills/harness-maintenance/
/.agents/skills/harness-maintenance/*
!/.agents/skills/harness-maintenance/SKILL.md

# ─── Confidential — never commit ─────────────────────────────
# Operator-local agent notes / personal overrides
CLAUDE.local.md
.agent-context/

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
!*.crt.example
.aws/
credentials

# WireGuard / PKI key material
wireguard/*.conf
wireguard/keys/
wireguard/config/
pki/

# ─── Terraform ────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
*.tfplan
crash.log

# ─── Build / language artifacts ───────────────────────────────
node_modules/
vendor/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
/bin/*
!/bin/check
# Default-deny above, one line per admitted script. bin/test is admitted because CI runs
# it, and a script the workflow calls but git does not carry fails a fresh clone with a
# missing-file error — which reads as a broken runner rather than as a missing line here.
!/bin/test
# bin/check-harness-block is admitted for the same reason, and it needs its own line:
# `!/bin/check` is an exact match, not a prefix — without this the harness audit would be
# untracked in every scaffolded repo, i.e. the audit would silently not exist.
!/bin/check-harness-block
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.test
*.out

# ─── Tooling / IDE / OS ───────────────────────────────────────
.claude/settings.local.json
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
*.log
